<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>About HelioForge Energy Lab | Author, Source &amp; Privacy</title><meta name="description" content="Learn who maintains HelioForge Energy Lab, where its source and methods live, and how the free MKGrid browser preview handles local progress."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta name="google-site-verification" content="wZk3bMiBHxDWxN4EmERLH9sBza2QlvsTaxbOSBncrvw"><meta name="author" content="Mohammad Rezwan Khan"><meta name="theme-color" content="#132923"><link rel="canonical" href="https://mkgrid.co.technology/about/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/domain.css"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:site_name" content="HelioForge"><meta property="og:title" content="About HelioForge Energy Lab | Author, Source &amp; Privacy"><meta property="og:description" content="Learn who maintains HelioForge Energy Lab, where its source and methods live, and how the free MKGrid browser preview handles local progress."><meta property="og:url" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/about/"><meta property="og:image" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/social-preview.png"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="HelioForge hybrid-energy research preview"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="About HelioForge Energy Lab | Author, Source &amp; Privacy"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Learn who maintains HelioForge Energy Lab, where its source and methods live, and how the free MKGrid browser preview handles local progress."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/social-preview.png"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#website","name":"HelioForge","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/","publisher":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},"inLanguage":"en"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/about/#page","name":"About HelioForge Energy Lab | Author, Source & Privacy","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/about/","description":"Learn who maintains HelioForge Energy Lab, where its source and methods live, and how the free MKGrid browser preview handles local progress.","inLanguage":"en","dateModified":"2026-10-26","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#website"},"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]}}]}</script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="/">H<span>↗</span> HelioForge</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="/run/">Open app</a><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a><a href="/about/">About</a></nav></header><main id="main"><article class="document"><p class="eyebrow">HELIOFORGE / ABOUT</p><h1>Energy research you can inspect.</h1><p class="lead">HelioForge Energy Lab is maintained by Mohammad Rezwan Khan as a hybrid-energy research and learning workbench.</p><h2>Author and public source</h2><p><a href="https://mrkhan.co.technology/">Mohammad Rezwan Khan’s profile</a> identifies the maintainer. The <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab">public repository</a> contains source, numerical methodology, lessons, validation records and contribution guidance. First-party source is available under the MIT license; bundled material retains its applicable notices.</p><h2>What MKGrid provides</h2><p>MKGrid hosts HelioForge’s free browser preview: architecture exploration, learning activities and bundled scenario results. It does not expose a public Python API. The Terminal workbench supports new bounded browser calculations. Advanced studies and optimization require the separate local application and its setup. The preview has no account or sign-in.</p><h2>Privacy and local state</h2><p>Supported browser progress remains local to this origin and device. The application has no external analytics scripts or external AI calls. Cloudflare delivers the website and processes normal web requests. Browser saves from MKLab or another domain do not automatically transfer here. Export supported local records before clearing browser storage.</p><h2>Questions and corrections</h2><p>Follow the repository’s <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/SUPPORT.md">support guide</a> for questions and <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security reporting instructions</a> for vulnerabilities. The <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> explains the scope of the hosted preview.</p><p>Explore the wider <a href="https://mklab.co.technology/">MKLab browser collection</a> or the separate <a href="https://khanlab.co.technology/">Datacenter Twin Lab course</a>.</p></article></main><footer><a class="wordmark" href="/">HelioForge</a><p>Explore energy systems. Inspect their assumptions.</p><a href="https://mklab.co.technology/">Explore MKLab apps →</a></footer></body></html>